{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48227", "qid": "gen-concept-2fe24307", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many analyses estimate the background ZZ irreducible background?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 31 analyses that estimate the ZZ irreducible background or related backgrounds. \n\nTo provide more context, here are the specific backgrounds included in this count:\n- ZZ irreducible background\n- WZ irreducible background\n- ttZ irreducible background\n- ttZ and tZq irreducible background\n- Xγ (photon conversion, mainly Zγ) irreducible background\n- ZZ/H production background\n- ZZ+jets background (ZZ+b, ZZ+c, ZZ+l)\n- ZZ and WZ diboson background (multilepton)\n- Diboson (WW, WZ, ZZ) background\n- Other multiboson background (ZZ, W±W±, VVV)\n- Z+jets background\n- tZq background\n- Z->tau+tau- background\n- Non-WW diboson background (WZ/γ*, ZZ/γ*, Wγ, Zγ)\n- Rare irreducible SM backgrounds (triboson, Higgs, other rare processes)\n- Zγ (photon conversion) background\n- t̄tZ background\n- Z -> tau tau background\n- Multiboson background\n- WZ + jets background\n\nIf you need more details on any specific background, let me know!\n\nAnswer: 31 analyses estimate the ZZ irreducible background or related backgrounds.\nAnswerable: true\nReason: answered", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2208.12095", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2404.06204", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "ZZ irreducible background", "kind