{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48227", "qid": "gen-conceptset-0640defb", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses report the systematic uncertainty Signal total cross-section theory uncertainty?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 46 distinct analyses that report the systematic uncertainty \"Signal total cross-section theory uncertainty\" or similar phrasings.\n\nTo provide more context, here are some of the specific phrasings found:\n\n- \"Signal total cross-section theory uncertainty\"\n- \"Total cross section theory uncertainty\"\n- \"Signal cross-section uncertainty\"\n- \"Signal theory uncertainty\"\n- \"Theoretical uncertainty on signal (Higgs production cross-section)\"\n- \"Total unfolding uncertainty in differential cross section measurement\"\n- \"Single-top production cross-section uncertainty\"\n- \"W+jets cross-section uncertainty\"\n- \"Pileup reweighting uncertainty (total inelastic cross section)\"\n- \"Wt inclusive cross-section normalisation uncertainty\"\n- \"Signal acceptance theory uncertainty\"\n- \"Pileup (inelastic pp cross section) uncertainty on signal yield\"\n- \"Theoretical uncertainty (PDF and renormalization/factorization scales) on signal production cross section\"\n- \"Total systematic uncertainty on the combined inclusive \\( t\\bar{t}Z \\) cross section\"\n- \"ttbar theory uncertainty\"\n- \"W(lnu) cross-section and acceptance uncertainty in CR_ttbar\"\n- \"Uncertainty from varying factorization and renormalization scales in signal cross section prediction\"\n- \"VBF, VH, ttH cross-section and acceptance uncertainties\"\n- \"ttbar+Z theory uncertainty\"\n- \"Inclusive signal/background cross section normalization uncertainty (scale, PDF+alphaS)\"\n- \"Diboson cross-section theoretical uncertainty\"\n- \"Statistical uncertainty of background contributions in cross section ratio measurement\"\n- \"Diboson cross-section normalisation uncertainty (6%)\"\n\nThese uncertainties are reported across various analyses, indicating the importance of accounting for theoretical uncertainties in the interpretation of results. \n\nIf you need more detailed information on specific analyses or further breakdowns, please let me know.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2009.04363", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2207.12246", "2208.12095", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2511.11853", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2604.27044", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Signal total cross-section theory uncertainty", "kind": "systematic_uncertainty"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.353}, {"round": 2, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "result_has_systematic", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.069}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:syst:factorization_renormalization_scale", "hepkg:syst:jet_energy_scale", "hepkg:syst:pileup_reweighting", "hepkg:systematic:background-stat-ratio", "hepkg:systematic:background-total-uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:cross-section-normalisation", "hepkg:systematic:diboson_cross_section_theory", "hepkg:systematic:diboson_normalisation", "hepkg:systematic:electron_total_systematic", "hepkg:systematic:ew_ttbar_cross_section", "hepkg:systematic:factorization-renormalization-scale", "hepkg:systematic:ggf-xsec-acceptance", "hepkg:systematic:ggf_hh_pdf_3pct", "hepkg:systematic:inclusive_cross_sections", 