{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48227", "qid": "gen-conceptset-6c12701d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define a region requiring Secondary vertex (SV)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define a region requiring a secondary vertex (SV):\n\n- **2004.01678**: Preselection region (m_llj < 250 GeV)\n- **2009.14537**: Preselection region (opposite-charge same-flavor dilepton, Z-veto, low p_T^ll)\n- **2012.01581**: Common dijet/SV preselection region (Table 2)\n- **2107.12553**: Baseline preselection common to all signal regions (Table 6)\n- **2304.08962**: Signal region (SR): tight vertex, m4mu<11 GeV, ΔR<0.25\n- **2401.07090**: Electron channel baseline preselection (B+ mass 4.7-5.7 GeV, prior to q^2 binning)\n- **2403.01556**: Generic emerging-jet signal region (>=2 tagged EJs)\n- **2404.06204**: Detector-level signal regions for W -> e nu, W -> mu nu, Z -> ee, and Z -> mu mu selections\n- **2508.13900**: Common preselection region (all channels), 0L, 0 S-jet category, 0L, 1 S-jet category, 1L, 0 S-jet category, 1L, 1 S-jet category, 2L, 0 S-jet category, and model-independent superbin: SV\n\nThese analyses cover a variety of final states and regions, each requiring a secondary vertex as part of their selection criteria.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2112.00895", "2205.05120", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2211.08028", "2304.08962", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2401.07090", "2403.01556", "2404.06204", "2407.10549", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Secondary vertex (SV)", "kind": "detector_object"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds":