{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48227", "qid": "gen-conceptset-99be86b0", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses measured Jet multiplicity (N_jets)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "hard", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses measured Jet multiplicity (N_jets):\n\n1. **2309.14442**: \"Inclusive and differential cross section measurements of ${{\\mathup{{{t}}}}{}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}}{\\mathup{{{b}}}}{\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\\\mathup{{{b}}}}}}}}}$ production in the lepton+jets channel at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\"\n2. **2401.05299**: \"Absolute differential cross-section vs $N_{\\mathrm{jets}}$ result\" and \"$A_{\\mathrm{C}}^{\\\\mathrm{rel}}$ vs $N_{\\mathrm{jets}}$ result\"\n3. **2402.08486**: \"Differential cross section measurements for the production of top quark pairs and of additional jets using dilepton events from ${\\mathup{{{p}}}}{\\mathup{{{p}}}}$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\"\n4. **2508.13900**: \"General search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{Te\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$\"\n\nThese papers cover various aspects of jet multiplicity in different contexts, including differential cross sections and relative charge asymmetry.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2110.11231", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2511.11853"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Jet multiplicity (N_jets)", "kind": "observable"}, "rows": 33, "error": null, "seconds": 0.318}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_measures_observable", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 56, "error": null, "seconds": 0.042}, {"round": 3, "tool": "papers