{"run_id": "20260803T234732-hepkg-48227", "qid": "gen-conceptset-ee151c7d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses report the systematic uncertainty PDF modelling uncertainty (CT14, MMHT2014 vs NNPDF3.0 replicas)?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "merged_entities"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 47 analyses that report the systematic uncertainty \"PDF modelling uncertainty (CT14, MMHT2014 vs NNPDF3.0 replicas)\" or related uncertainties. Here are some of the specific analyses and the exact uncertainties they report:\n\n1. **Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}\\)**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n2. **Combined measurements and interpretations of Higgs boson production and decay in proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}\\)**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n   - PDF choice and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty\n\n3. **Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using \\(H \\rightarrow b\\bar{b}\\) decays in the ATLAS detector**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n\n4. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions using the final state in proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}\\)**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n5. **Differential cross section measurements for the production of top quark pairs and of additional jets using dilepton events from \\(pp\\) collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}\\)**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n6. **Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons and the top quark**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n   - PDF choice and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty\n\n7. **Evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n8. **Evidence for the charge asymmetry in \\(pp \\rightarrow t\\bar{t}\\) production at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\) TeV with the ATLAS detector**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n   - PDF envelope (CT14, MMHT2014) uncertainty in charge asymmetry prediction\n\n9. **Fiducial WZ production cross section measurement (combined flavour categories)**:\n   - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n   - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n10. **General search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s}=13\\,\\text{TeV}\\)**:\n    - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n    - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n11. **Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 \\(b\\) final state**:\n    - PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n    - PDF and renormalization/factorization scale uncertainty\n\n12. **Inclusive and differential cross section measurements of \\(t\\bar{t}b", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2009.04363", "2010.14293", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.